# What this plugin is, for the index in README.md and for whoever installs
# it alone. One key per line, a key repeated for each line of a message;
# ./install.sh at the repository's top installs it from the lines below.
name: xymonapi
version: 3.0.1
side: server, client
summary: a read-only HTTP and JSON interface to a Xymon server, as one of its xymonlaunch tasks, and its client
requires: python >= 3.9
xymon: 4.3.31
manual: xymonapi.8

# How ./install.sh installs it. server-* and tools-* are each side's: the
# files copied beside the plugin's others, the manual page, the modules its
# Python needs (offered at install time), the plugins it needs first.
# xymon is the lowest Xymon its server side works with.
# executable lists the files made 755, the others 644; command is the
# tools' command in $PREFIX/bin and the script it runs; task, conf and
# restart are the server's xymonlaunch task, web server snippets kept once
# written, and the program whose running process an install stops. The
# messages may name @ETC@, @TASKDIR@ and @XYMONHOME@.
server-files: app.py xymon.py xymonapi_client.py tokens.py openapi.yaml requirements.txt xymonapi.sh
server-manual: xymonapi.8
server-modules: fastapi uvicorn yaml
task: xymonapi.tasks.DIST
conf: xymonapi-apache.conf xymonapi-nginx.conf xymonapi-lighttpd.conf
restart: app.py
installed: Installed. For other machines, include @XYMONHOME@/ext/xymonapi/xymonapi-{apache,nginx,lighttpd}.conf in the web server,
installed:   so that it is skipped once gone -- IncludeOptional on Apache, a wildcard (xymonapi-nginx*.conf) on nginx and lighttpd --
installed:   or give the API xymond's certificate: see xymonapi(8).
installed: It starts only with its users' passwords: @ETC@/xymonpasswd, the web pages' own, or another file in XYMONAPI_PASSWD.
uninstalled: Uninstalled xymonapi. Its web server snippets went with ext/xymonapi, which an IncludeOptional or a wildcard include skips.
uninstalled:   Kept: the tokens file, $XYMONAPI_TOKENS ($XYMONVAR/xymonapi/tokens by default), and any snippet an older install
uninstalled:   left in @ETC@, yours to remove once no Include names it.
tools-files: xymonapi_client.py xymonapi-connect.sh
tools-manual: xymonapi-connect.1
command: xymonapi-connect xymonapi-connect.sh
executable: xymonapi.sh xymonapi-connect.sh
uninstalled-tools: Uninstalled xymonapi's client. Kept: the tokens in ~/.config/xymon-api/, which the API's /tokens revokes.
